# Graphene monolayer, a = 2.48 Ang (the in-plane equilibrium lattice constant of this level of
# theory: GGA-PBE, TZP, virtual_vault Troullier-Martins carbon; an energy-vs-a scan puts the minimum
# at 2.4815 Ang, reference_results/graphene/a0_scan.csv), 20 Ang cell along c => ~16.6 Ang of
# vacuum. The two C atoms are fixed by symmetry, so no position relaxation is needed: this IS the
# already-relaxed structure stb-optical takes. 2D (one vacuum axis); hexagonal P6/mmm => two
# independent tensor components, eps_xx = eps_yy (in-plane) and eps_zz (out-of-plane):
# --directions xx zz is enough.
SystemName graphene
SystemLabel siesta

NumberOfSpecies 1
%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1  6  C
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang
%block LatticeVectors
  2.480000   0.000000   0.000000
 -1.240000   2.147741   0.000000
  0.000000   0.000000  20.000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

NumberOfAtoms 2
AtomicCoordinatesFormat Fractional
%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
 0.333333333  0.666666667  0.5  1
 0.666666667  0.333333333  0.5  1
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
